  <content>
<procedure>
<preliminaryRqmts>
<reqCondGroup>
<reqCondDm><reqCond>The used filter element is removed.</reqCond><dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="40" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="02" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="520" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef></reqCondDm>
</reqCondGroup>
<reqSupportEquips><noSupportEquips/></reqSupportEquips>
<reqSupplies><supplyDescrGroup><supplyDescr id="sup-0001"><name>Lint-free cloth</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="LINT-FREE-CLOTH" supplyNumberType="sp05"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr>
<supplyDescr id="sup-0002"><name>Hydraulic oil, HLP 46</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="DIN 51524-2 HLP 46" supplyNumberType="sp02"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr>
</supplyDescrGroup></reqSupplies>
<reqSpares><spareDescrGroup>
<spareDescr id="spa-0001"><name>Filter element, 10 micrometers</name><identNumber><manufacturerCode>VH000</manufacturerCode><partAndSerialNumber><partNumber>VH15-4002</partNumber></partAndSerialNumber></identNumber><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></spareDescr>
</spareDescrGroup></reqSpares>
<reqSafety><safetyRqmts>
<warning><warningAndCautionPara>Hydraulic oil can be hot. Let the unit become cool to less than 40 °C before you start this procedure. Hot oil can cause burns.</warningAndCautionPara></warning>
<warning><warningAndCautionPara>Make sure that the system pressure is 0 bar. Oil under pressure can cause serious injury.</warningAndCautionPara></warning>
<caution><warningAndCautionPara>Do not let dirt into the filter housing. Dirt in the hydraulic oil can cause damage to the pump and the valves.</warningAndCautionPara></caution>
</safetyRqmts></reqSafety>
</preliminaryRqmts>
<mainProcedure>
<proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the part number on the new filter element is VH15-4002.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Apply a thin layer of clean hydraulic oil to the seal of the new filter element.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Put the filter element into the housing. Push the element down until it is fully seated.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Install the filter cover. Turn the cover clockwise until it is tight by hand. Do not use tools.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Remove the lint-free cloths.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Start the hydraulic power unit and let it operate without load for 5 minutes.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Examine the filter cover for leaks. If there is a leak, stop the unit and tighten the cover by hand.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the clogging indicator shows green.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Stop the unit. Examine the oil level on the level gauge. If the level is low, add oil: <dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="10" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="241" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>.</para></proceduralStep>
</mainProcedure>
<closeRqmts><reqCondGroup>
<reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The return filter is serviceable.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef>
</reqCondGroup></closeRqmts>
</procedure>
</content>
